The group comparison is done in the same way as a dummy code is done in regression - there is one reference group and all of the other group means are shown as the difference from the reference group.

To compare the intercepts and means in each group you can name the parameters, and then use generate new parameters.

(untested code, from memory - if you can provide a reproducible example, we can test)
# sets up the four group intercepts
i  ~ c(g1_int, g2_int, g3_int, g4_int) * groups
# set up a parameter that is the difference between the intercepts of groups 2 and 3.
g2_3_int_diff := g_2_int - g_3_int

